{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","title":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII.md","line":374,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII.tex#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","line":852,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[nearby maps are homotopic]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0496,petersen:page-0497}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular, lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma}\n  \\dcref{ch12:12.6.4}\n  With $\\delta$ as in \\cref{lem:pet-ch12-alpha-regular-existence}, if\n  $f_0,f_1:X\\to M$ are continuous with $|f_0(x)f_1(x)|<\\delta$ for all $x\\in X$,\n  then $f_0,f_1$ are homotopic.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic,cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular,lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular}, the diagonal neighborhood is\n  \\(\\alpha\\)-regular, so the retraction lemma\n  supplies a continuous deformation to \\(\\Delta\\). Its flow paths induce\n  continuous curves \\(H(p,q,t)\\) from \\(p\\) to \\(q\\) of length at most\n  \\(C|pq|\\), with \\(C=\\sqrt2/\\cos\\alpha\\). Applying \\(H\\) pointwise to\n  \\(f_0(x),f_1(x)\\) gives the homotopy.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[nearby maps are homotopic] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d636831322d636c6f73652d6d6170732d686f6d6f746f706963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0496, petersen:page-0497</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23cor%3Apet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular\">↗ cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23lem%3Apet-ch12-retraction-lemma\">↗ lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch12:12.6.4</span></span>With <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\delta $\">$\\delta $</span> as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23lem%3Apet-ch12-alpha-regular-existence\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-alpha-regular-existence\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d636831322d616c7068612d726567756c61722d6578697374656e6365\">section 6</a>, if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_0,f_1:X\\to M$\">$f_0,f_1:X\\to M$</span> are continuous with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|f_0(x)f_1(x)|&lt;\\delta $\">$|f_0(x)f_1(x)|&lt;\\delta $</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\in X$\">$x\\in X$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_0,f_1$\">$f_0,f_1$</span> are homotopic.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23cor%3Apet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic\">↗ cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23cor%3Apet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular\">↗ cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23lem%3Apet-ch12-retraction-lemma\">↗ lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma</a> \\sketch By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII%23cor%3Apet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d636831322d646961676f6e616c2d616c7068612d726567756c6172\">section 6</a>, the diagonal neighborhood is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\alpha $\">$\\alpha $</span>-regular, so the retraction lemma supplies a continuous deformation to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Delta $\">$\\Delta $</span>. Its flow paths induce continuous curves <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H(p,q,t)$\">$H(p,q,t)$</span> from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span> of length at most <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C|pq|$\">$C|pq|$</span>, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C=\\sqrt2/\\cos \\alpha $\">$C=\\sqrt2/\\cos \\alpha $</span>. Applying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H$\">$H$</span> pointwise to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_0(x),f_1(x)$\">$f_0(x),f_1(x)$</span> gives the homotopy. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-simplex-extension","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular","title":"cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular","label":"cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma","title":"lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma","label":"lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","title":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","label":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","title":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","label":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-simplex-extension","title":"lem:pet-ch12-simplex-extension","label":"lem:pet-ch12-simplex-extension"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-gh-close-homotopy-equivalent","title":"lem:pet-ch12-gh-close-homotopy-equivalent","label":"lem:pet-ch12-gh-close-homotopy-equivalent"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","title":"cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[nearby maps are homotopic]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0496,petersen:page-0497}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular, lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma}\n  \\dcref{ch12:12.6.4}\n  With $\\delta$ as in \\cref{lem:pet-ch12-alpha-regular-existence}, if\n  $f_0,f_1:X\\to M$ are continuous with $|f_0(x)f_1(x)|<\\delta$ for all $x\\in X$,\n  then $f_0,f_1$ are homotopic.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{cor:pet-ch12-close-maps-homotopic,cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular,lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular}, the diagonal neighborhood is\n  \\(\\alpha\\)-regular, so the retraction lemma\n  supplies a continuous deformation to \\(\\Delta\\). Its flow paths induce\n  continuous curves \\(H(p,q,t)\\) from \\(p\\) to \\(q\\) of length at most\n  \\(C|pq|\\), with \\(C=\\sqrt2/\\cos\\alpha\\). Applying \\(H\\) pointwise to\n  \\(f_0(x),f_1(x)\\) gives the homotopy.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular","title":"cor:pet-ch12-diagonal-alpha-regular","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch12_SectionalCurvatureComparisonII#lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma","title":"lem:pet-ch12-retraction-lemma","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}